+The native helper's final-iteration fallback can freeze records not selected by the sign rule. Exact helper correspondence therefore needs the final-iteration flag false, or a caller-history/count invariant that makes this fallback unreachable. For two valid records with (before,min,max)=(0,1,1) and (0,0,1), sign selection freezes only the first, while an arbitrary final-iteration invocation also freezes the second. ProgressTarget is a property of the sign selector; it does not by itself prove the required whole-loop invariant.
